edits.new:
Mounting the EVM on the CR covers the whole FC boost channel, which has an open undiagnosed fault.
- **Rejected zones re-assessed without a height limit (r7 review 7 close, D-H).** The operator statement of 2026-11-10 removes
  every maximum height for the MB and its PCBs. A raised stack, a taller header body or a taller connector therefore stops
  being an objection by itself. Each rejection is re-assessed on its remaining reasons (`round4/work/mb_mechanical.md`
  Table 1, `round4/work/proposal_evm_on_cr.md` section 2.1); no new layout is adopted:
  - the -x zone and the zone past x = 0 cover the J-BL/J-FC wire entries and screws and the J-NTC push buttons; a header body
    of >= 22.7 mm would clear the blocks in height, but not the access: still rejected;
  - the -y zone covers BAL pad 8 (T22, PM11), RB1A and CBL2 and lies 2.96 mm from VSW-BT; it had no height reason: still
    rejected;
  - the +y wide zone (x 17.70-48.70, y 67.14-76.51) had one height reason, a 2.75 mm header body over OP-FC. It still covers
    the FC droop analog (OP-FC, MDAC-FC, RD/RINJ and the VDROOP-FC, N$7 and N$8 nets) and blocks OP-FC and MDAC-FC, whose
    AD5443/OPA197 DMM block measurement is an open bench item: still rejected;
  - the +y and -y zones to the MB edge lie over a boost switching node (L-FC, REG-FC and VSW-FC; L-BT, REG-BT and VSW-BT) and
    cover the boost, droop or BAL parts: still rejected;
  - the extension past x 65.00 is a 34.2 mm cantilever over the 16 V VBUS pour with its tip 0.5 mm from RENC2; it had no
    height reason: still rejected;
  - the EVM on the CR covers the FC boost channel and puts the EVM mass on the 22 pins; it had no height reason: still
    rejected;
  - the mezzanine over the MB loses its height objection; its remaining reasons still reject it for this round (J.2 item 61).

